  "body": "### Problem\n\nA routing group can choose a local provider configured with “Send requests unmasked”, but the request may still wait for a full masking pass because other members or fallback targets require masking. The successful attempt displayed in the request details can therefore be an unmasked provider while the request shows substantial masking time.\n\nObserved with a nested routing group and a remote classifier: a Chat request ultimately served by a local provider took 5.756 s, including 2.005 s of masking before the upstream attempt. The request used approximately 30k cached input tokens. The provider's unmasked setting was enabled. This is a separate case from #3973: that fix already skips masking when the entire route is unmasked.\n\n### Expected\n\nWhere feasible, defer full request masking until an attempt actually needs a masked body. An attempt to an unmasked provider should not have to wait for a full scan merely because a later fallback might require one. If a later attempt needs masking, mask before sending to it. The classifier is a separate recipient and must retain its own privacy protection; do not send it unmasked text without its own explicit setting.\n\n### Investigation\n\nIn current `serve`, `unredactedRoute` returns false if any possible member requires masking, so `redactedHits` runs before attempts. Classifier masking can also contribute to the same timing metric; the reported timing alone does not distinguish the two. Please preserve masking of remote classifiers, fallback attempts, observers and archives when considering a change.\n",
